# satellite_telemetry.md

This document outlines the **SatelliteTelemetrySystem** located under
`game/tracking/satellite/` used by the engine.
**Note:** All systems are modular and self-contained. See [docs/modular/game_system_tree.md](../modular/game_system_tree.md) for the latest status. A system remains **In-Progress** until its documentation, cleanup, and tests are merged and verified.


---

## Purpose

- Provide optional satellite tracking data for the Combat Simulation and other modules.
- Fetches JSON from a remote API using libcurl.
- Offers a simulation mode when network access is unavailable.

## Initialization

`SatelliteTelemetrySystem` is initialized with an API endpoint. If no endpoint is available you can supply a JSON string for offline testing.

> Public copy redacts internal telemetry endpoints. Contact operations for full endpoint list.

```cpp
#include "tracking/satellite/SatelliteTelemetrySystem.h"

game::SatelliteTelemetrySystem telemetry;
telemetry.initialize("[REDACTED: primary telemetry base URL]");
telemetry.setSimulatedResponse(R"({"id":"1","lat":0.0,"lon":0.0,"alt":420.0})");
```

## Fetch Example

```cpp
auto result = telemetry.fetch("SAT-2048");
if (result) {
    float lat = result->latitude;
    float lon = result->longitude;
    float alt = result->altitude;
}
```

The call requests the given satellite ID. If the network request fails it falls back to the simulated JSON.

## Engine Workflow

`SatelliteTelemetrySystem` implements `ITelemetrySource` and registers with
`TelemetryManager` during `Game::StartGame`.
The manager gathers packets every frame and forwards them to systems such as
`SpaceManager` or `CombatSimulator` for processing.

## Simulated Generator

When no network data is available, the system can produce synthetic
telemetry using `SatelliteTelemetryGenerator`. The generator supports
randomized values or a simple orbital model.

```cpp
game::TelemetryGenOptions opts;
opts.mode = game::TelemetryGenMode::Orbit;
opts.orbitInclination = 45.f;
telemetry.enableSimulation(opts);
```

Each call to `fetch` will advance the generator and return new latitude,
longitude and altitude values.
# Satellite Telemetry System (Public Edition)

This public note outlines the purpose of the SatelliteTelemetrySystem without disclosing proprietary networking or simulation details.

## Purpose
- Provide optional orbital tracking data to gameplay modules.
- Support both live API requests and offline simulation modes.

## Initialization & Usage
Systems can initialize the telemetry module with an endpoint or fallback data source. Concrete API shapes, authentication flows, and example payloads are **[REDACTED]**.

## Engine Workflow
Telemetry integrates with broader managers to distribute data where needed. Registration routines, threading behavior, and data retention policies are **[REDACTED]**.

## Simulation Support
A generator can supply synthetic orbital data when live feeds are unavailable. Parameter tuning, orbital math, and debugging commands are **[REDACTED]**.

## Summary
Consult the private repository for complete implementation details and operational checklists.
